      "created_at": "2022-02-08T19:26:00Z",
      "updated_at": "2022-02-08T19:26:00Z",
      "body": "Files are not deleted from the server mostly because it is easier (note I didn't say _better_) to err on the side of caution and keep everything.\r\n\r\nIt is probably better to update this logic so that when a post is purged, its associated uploads are also deleted. An additional ACP option to preserve the files would be better in cases where storage is not a concern.\r\n\r\nSecondly, re: the right to be forgotten (that is, deleting a user's own files on the server), the process to do this is to request account deletion from an admin. When an admin deletes your account, all of your content (topics, posts, uploads, etc.) are purged from the server.\r\n\r\n_Re: sorting of files in the ACP, open a new issue for this._",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
